# Phase 18 Common Message equality reverse-surface — 20261015T010606Z

- Compared Java 5.5.1 `Message`/`MessageExt` declarations with the Rust public surface. Java classes inherit identity-based `Object.equals`/`hashCode`; Rust had exposed field-based `PartialEq`/`Eq`.
- Removed structural equality from `Message`. `MessageExt` now compares a private identity token; cloning preserves that token, and serde skips it so each deserialized object receives a fresh identity. The Java `messagePublicApi` fixture records same-instance and distinct-default outcomes. A compile-fail doctest guards `Message`'s missing structural equality; Rust fixture tests cover `MessageExt` identity behavior.
- Updated Phase 6/8 compatibility maps and the release checklist. Fixture SHA-256: `689666cff0ba5319cbe396e5a20a6b5943d1e23fc394299c7f69d22b65a4ed42`.
